concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-14-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "14(4) Controlled carriage services, controlled networks and controlled"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-14-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) For the purposes of this section, a telecommunications network, or a facility, satisfies the geographical test if:  (a) the whole or any part of the network or facility, as the case requires, is, or will be, located in Australia; or  (b) all of the following conditions are satisfied:  (i) a person, or a group of persons, operates the network or the facility, as the case requires;  (ii) the person, or at least one of the members of the group, carries on, or will carry on, a telecommunications-related business wholly or partly in Australia;  (iii) the network, or the facility, as the case requires, is used, or will be used, to supply a listed carriage service, or a service that is ancillary or incidental to such a service. Definition" ;
    skos:definition "(4) For the purposes of this section, a telecommunications network, or a facility, satisfies the geographical test if:  (a) the whole or any part of the network or facility, as the case requires, is, or will be, located in Australia; or  (b) all of the following conditions are satisfied:  (i) a person, or a group of persons, operates the network or the facility, as the case requires;  (ii) the person, or at least one of the members of the group, carries on, or will carry on, a telecommunications-related business wholly or partly in Australia;  (iii) the network, or the facility, as the case requires, is used, or will be used, to supply a listed carriage service, or a service that is ancillary or incidental to such a service. Definition"@en ;
