doc:sec-33-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "33(2) Intercell hand-over functions" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) For the purposes of this section, a carriage service is an eligible mobile telecommunications service if:  (a) an end-user can use it while moving continuously between places; and   Network units  Part 2 Related definitions  Division 3  Section 34  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (b) customer equipment used for or in relation to the supply of the service is not in physical contact with any part of the telecommunications network by means of which the service is supplied. 34  When a base station is part of a terrestrial radiocommunications customer access network" ;
    cof:pageNumber "62"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-33-ss-1 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "33(1) Intercell hand-over functions"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-33-ss-1 ;
    values:originalText "(1) For the purposes of this Act, a base station is part of a terrestrial radiocommunications customer access network if, and only if:  (a) the base station is part of a telecommunications network; and  (b) the base station is not an exempt base station (as defined by subsection (2)); and  (c) the base station is used, or for use, in connection with the supply of a carriage service; and  (d) customer equipment used for or in relation to the supply of the service is not in physical contact with any part of the telecommunications network by means of which the service is supplied; and  (e) the service is wholly or principally used, or wholly or principally for use, by each end-user:  (i) at premises occupied or used by the end-user; or  (ii) in the immediate vicinity of those premises; and  (f) the network does not have intercell hand-over functions; and  (g) the conditions (if any) specified in the regulations are satisfied; and  (h) the network is not an exempt network (as defined by subsection (3))." ;
    skos:definition "(1) For the purposes of this Act, a base station is part of a terrestrial radiocommunications customer access network if, and only if:  (a) the base station is part of a telecommunications network; and  (b) the base station is not an exempt base station (as defined by subsection (2)); and  (c) the base station is used, or for use, in connection with the supply of a carriage service; and  (d) customer equipment used for or in relation to the supply of the service is not in physical contact with any part of the telecommunications network by means of which the service is supplied; and  (e) the service is wholly or principally used, or wholly or principally for use, by each end-user:  (i) at premises occupied or used by the end-user; or  (ii) in the immediate vicinity of those premises; and  (f) the network does not have intercell hand-over functions; and  (g) the conditions (if any) specified in the regulations are satisfied; and  (h) the network is not an exempt network (as defined by subsection (3))."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ae34369e6bbc0277f8831cf837121aec8557b4a7c353a532dfe93975a00efcb9" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-33 ;
    cof:pageNumber "62"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Telecommunications network must have intercell hand-over functions if it meets certain conditions. Base station must be part of a terrestrial customer access network under specific conditions." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
