concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-36-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "36(3) Distinct places—basic rules"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-36-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) Places are in the same area if they are situated in properties each of which forms part of a combined area as defined by section 38 and:  (a) the same person or persons is or are the principal user (as defined by section 39) of all the properties that together constitute that combined area; or  (b) because of a determination in force under section 40, that combined area is an eligible combined area for the purposes of this paragraph." ;
    skos:definition "(3) Places are in the same area if they are situated in properties each of which forms part of a combined area as defined by section 38 and:  (a) the same person or persons is or are the principal user (as defined by section 39) of all the properties that together constitute that combined area; or  (b) because of a determination in force under section 40, that combined area is an eligible combined area for the purposes of this paragraph."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "c539082777a6d79c305d3cd3a7acd3ad62d630812c9585b7bd5920def5b2ec39" ;
