concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-39 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "39 Principal user of a property"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-39 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The principal user of a property is the person who:  (a) occupies the property; or  (b) uses the property for the purpose that is the sole or principal purpose for which the property is used.  (2) However, if 2 or more persons:  (a) together occupy a property; or  (b) together use a property for the purpose that is the sole or principal purpose for which the property is used; they are taken to together be the principal user of the property." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The principal user of a property is the person who:  (a) occupies the property; or  (b) uses the property for the purpose that is the sole or principal purpose for which the property is used.  (2) However, if 2 or more persons:  (a) together occupy a property; or  (b) together use a property for the purpose that is the sole or principal purpose for which the property is used; they are taken to together be the principal user of the property."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "49d6a735f359ac36686d54ae1d7bded16089b7b2555b666f8c291dc6df5dce8a" ;
    cof:pageNumber "68"^^xsd:integer ;
