    cof:pageNumber "96"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-63 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "63 Conditions of carrier licence declared by Minister"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-63 ;
    values:originalText "Conditions applying to each carrier licence  (1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, declare that each carrier licence is subject to such conditions as are specified in the instrument.   Carriers  Part 3 Carrier licences  Division 3  Section 63  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  Conditions applying to specified existing carrier licences  (2) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, declare that a specified carrier licence is subject to such conditions as are specified in the instrument. Note: A licence may be specified by name, by inclusion in a specified class or in any other way. Conditions applying to specified future carrier licences  (3) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, declare that, in the event that a carrier licence is granted to a specified person during a specified period, the carrier licence is subject to such conditions as are specified in the instrument. Declarations have effect  (4) A declaration under this section has effect accordingly. Variation of conditions  (5) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, vary an instrument under subsection (1), (2) or (3). Revocation of conditions  (6) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, revoke an instrument under subsection (1), (2) or (3). Notification of conditions—existing licences  (7) As soon as practicable after the Minister makes an instrument under subsection (1), (2), (5) or (6) that relates to a licence, the Minister must give the holder of the licence a copy of the instrument." ;
    skos:definition "Conditions applying to each carrier licence  (1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, declare that each carrier licence is subject to such conditions as are specified in the instrument.   Carriers  Part 3 Carrier licences  Division 3  Section 63  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  Conditions applying to specified existing carrier licences  (2) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, declare that a specified carrier licence is subject to such conditions as are specified in the instrument. Note: A licence may be specified by name, by inclusion in a specified class or in any other way. Conditions applying to specified future carrier licences  (3) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, declare that, in the event that a carrier licence is granted to a specified person during a specified period, the carrier licence is subject to such conditions as are specified in the instrument. Declarations have effect  (4) A declaration under this section has effect accordingly. Variation of conditions  (5) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, vary an instrument under subsection (1), (2) or (3). Revocation of conditions  (6) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, revoke an instrument under subsection (1), (2) or (3). Notification of conditions—existing licences  (7) As soon as practicable after the Minister makes an instrument under subsection (1), (2), (5) or (6) that relates to a licence, the Minister must give the holder of the licence a copy of the instrument."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "a593d5f13ca520adff6c002b87472cef5d1f053c12a29c67584dd3c14e4833af" ;
    cof:pageNumber "96"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-63-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-63-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-63-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-63-ss-4 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-63-ss-5 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-63-ss-6 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-63-ss-7 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-act-1997.pdf> ;
    dc:source "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.96" .
doc:sec-63 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "63 Conditions of carrier licence declared by Minister" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Conditions applying to each carrier licence  (1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, declare that each carrier licence is subject to such conditions as are specified in the instrument.   Carriers  Part 3 Carrier licences  Division 3  Section 63  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  Conditions applying to specified existing carrier licences  (2) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, declare that a specified carrier licence is subject to such conditions as are specified in the instrument. Note: A licence may be specified by name, by inclusion in a specified class or in any other way. Conditions applying to specified future carrier licences  (3) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, declare that, in the event that a carrier licence is granted to a specified person during a specified period, the carrier licence is subject to such conditions as are specified in the instrument. Declarations have effect  (4) A declaration under this section has effect accordingly. Variation of conditions  (5) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, vary an instrument under subsection (1), (2) or (3). Revocation of conditions  (6) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, revoke an instrument under subsection (1), (2) or (3). Notification of conditions—existing licences  (7) As soon as practicable after the Minister makes an instrument under subsection (1), (2), (5) or (6) that relates to a licence, the Minister must give the holder of the licence a copy of the instrument." ;
    cof:pageNumber "96"^^xsd:integer .

