doc:sec-72-ss-2b a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "72(2B) Cancellation of carrier licence" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2B) The ACMA may cancel a carrier licence held by a carrier if the carrier fails to pay in full any funding charge on or before the date on which the funding charge becomes due and payable. For this purpose, funding charge means charge imposed by the Telecommunications (Regional Broadband Scheme) Charge Act 2020. Becoming a disqualified body corporate" ;
    cof:pageNumber "108"^^xsd:integer .

