concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-73 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "73 Collection of charges relating to carrier licences"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-73 ;
    values:originalText "Definitions  (1) In this section: annual charge means charge imposed by Part 3 of the Telecommunications (Carrier Licence Charges) Act 1997. application charge means charge imposed by Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Carrier Licence Charges) Act 1997. late payment penalty means an amount that is payable by way of penalty in accordance with a determination under subsection (4).   Carriers  Part 3 Carrier licences  Division 3  Section 73  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  When application charge due and payable  (2) Application charge imposed on an application for a carrier licence is due and payable when the application is made. When annual charge due and payable  (3) Annual charge is due and payable at the time ascertained in accordance with a written determination made by the ACMA. Late payment penalty  (4) The ACMA may, by written instrument, determine that, if any annual charge payable by a person remains unpaid after the time when it became due for payment, the person is liable to pay to the Commonwealth, by way of penalty, an amount calculated at the rate of:  (a) 20% per annum; or  (b) if the determination specifies a lower percentage—that lower percentage per annum; on the amount unpaid, computed from that time. Determination has effect  (5) A determination under subsection (4) has effect accordingly. Remission of penalty  (6) A determination under subsection (4) may authorise the ACMA to make decisions about the remission of the whole or a part of an amount of late payment penalty. Payment of charge and late payment penalty  (7) Annual charge, application charge and late payment penalty are payable to the ACMA on behalf of the Commonwealth." ;
    skos:definition "Definitions  (1) In this section: annual charge means charge imposed by Part 3 of the Telecommunications (Carrier Licence Charges) Act 1997. application charge means charge imposed by Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Carrier Licence Charges) Act 1997. late payment penalty means an amount that is payable by way of penalty in accordance with a determination under subsection (4).   Carriers  Part 3 Carrier licences  Division 3  Section 73  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  When application charge due and payable  (2) Application charge imposed on an application for a carrier licence is due and payable when the application is made. When annual charge due and payable  (3) Annual charge is due and payable at the time ascertained in accordance with a written determination made by the ACMA. Late payment penalty  (4) The ACMA may, by written instrument, determine that, if any annual charge payable by a person remains unpaid after the time when it became due for payment, the person is liable to pay to the Commonwealth, by way of penalty, an amount calculated at the rate of:  (a) 20% per annum; or  (b) if the determination specifies a lower percentage—that lower percentage per annum; on the amount unpaid, computed from that time. Determination has effect  (5) A determination under subsection (4) has effect accordingly. Remission of penalty  (6) A determination under subsection (4) may authorise the ACMA to make decisions about the remission of the whole or a part of an amount of late payment penalty. Payment of charge and late payment penalty  (7) Annual charge, application charge and late payment penalty are payable to the ACMA on behalf of the Commonwealth."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "8775bbb39cb0805e30a731b00808ae5b246fcde24b445f1734656bf34ac5e2af" ;
    cof:pageNumber "110"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-73-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-73-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-73-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-73-ss-4 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-73-ss-5 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-73-ss-6 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-73-ss-7 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-act-1997.pdf> ;
    dc:source "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.110" .
doc:sec-73 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "73 Collection of charges relating to carrier licences" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Definitions  (1) In this section: annual charge means charge imposed by Part 3 of the Telecommunications (Carrier Licence Charges) Act 1997. application charge means charge imposed by Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Carrier Licence Charges) Act 1997. late payment penalty means an amount that is payable by way of penalty in accordance with a determination under subsection (4).   Carriers  Part 3 Carrier licences  Division 3  Section 73  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  When application charge due and payable  (2) Application charge imposed on an application for a carrier licence is due and payable when the application is made. When annual charge due and payable  (3) Annual charge is due and payable at the time ascertained in accordance with a written determination made by the ACMA. Late payment penalty  (4) The ACMA may, by written instrument, determine that, if any annual charge payable by a person remains unpaid after the time when it became due for payment, the person is liable to pay to the Commonwealth, by way of penalty, an amount calculated at the rate of:  (a) 20% per annum; or  (b) if the determination specifies a lower percentage—that lower percentage per annum; on the amount unpaid, computed from that time. Determination has effect  (5) A determination under subsection (4) has effect accordingly. Remission of penalty  (6) A determination under subsection (4) may authorise the ACMA to make decisions about the remission of the whole or a part of an amount of late payment penalty. Payment of charge and late payment penalty  (7) Annual charge, application charge and late payment penalty are payable to the ACMA on behalf of the Commonwealth." ;
    cof:pageNumber "110"^^xsd:integer .

