concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-96 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "96 Exemption from certain regulatory provisions—Ministerial"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-96 ;
    values:originalText "determination  (1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that a specified regulatory provision does not apply to a specified person in the person’s capacity as a designated carriage service provider. For this purpose, a designated carriage service provider is a person who is a carriage service provider under subsection 87(4) or (5). Note: For specification by class, see subsection 13(3) of the Legislation Act 2003.  (2) A determination under this section may be unconditional or subject to such conditions (if any) as are specified in the determination.  (3) A determination under this section has effect accordingly.  (5) For the purposes of this section, a regulatory provision is a provision of:  (a) this Act; or  (b) any other law of the Commonwealth; that contains a reference to a carriage service provider or to carriage service providers.   Service providers  Part 4 Content service providers  Division 4  Section 97  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026" ;
    skos:definition "determination  (1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that a specified regulatory provision does not apply to a specified person in the person’s capacity as a designated carriage service provider. For this purpose, a designated carriage service provider is a person who is a carriage service provider under subsection 87(4) or (5). Note: For specification by class, see subsection 13(3) of the Legislation Act 2003.  (2) A determination under this section may be unconditional or subject to such conditions (if any) as are specified in the determination.  (3) A determination under this section has effect accordingly.  (5) For the purposes of this section, a regulatory provision is a provision of:  (a) this Act; or  (b) any other law of the Commonwealth; that contains a reference to a carriage service provider or to carriage service providers.   Service providers  Part 4 Content service providers  Division 4  Section 97  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "95f1a23373195c7816d78c02422e5944df04440e32be8972aa51a82f68c57237" ;
    cof:pageNumber "128"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-96-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-96-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-96-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-96-ss-5 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-act-1997.pdf> ;
    dc:source "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.128" .
doc:sec-96 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "96 Exemption from certain regulatory provisions—Ministerial" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "determination  (1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that a specified regulatory provision does not apply to a specified person in the person’s capacity as a designated carriage service provider. For this purpose, a designated carriage service provider is a person who is a carriage service provider under subsection 87(4) or (5). Note: For specification by class, see subsection 13(3) of the Legislation Act 2003.  (2) A determination under this section may be unconditional or subject to such conditions (if any) as are specified in the determination.  (3) A determination under this section has effect accordingly.  (5) For the purposes of this section, a regulatory provision is a provision of:  (a) this Act; or  (b) any other law of the Commonwealth; that contains a reference to a carriage service provider or to carriage service providers.   Service providers  Part 4 Content service providers  Division 4  Section 97  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026" ;
    cof:pageNumber "128"^^xsd:integer .

