concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-100 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "100 Exemptions from service provider rules"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-100 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that a specified service provider is exempt from the service provider rules.  (2) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that a specified service provider is exempt from a specified service provider rule.  (3) A determination under this section may be unconditional or subject to such conditions (if any) as are specified in the determination.  (4) A determination under this section has effect accordingly." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that a specified service provider is exempt from the service provider rules.  (2) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that a specified service provider is exempt from a specified service provider rule.  (3) A determination under this section may be unconditional or subject to such conditions (if any) as are specified in the determination.  (4) A determination under this section has effect accordingly."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "0188a2e80d1e20edb410cbee6f03836e933f3533667abea9a0693d2ddde2a1b0" ;
    cof:pageNumber "132"^^xsd:integer ;
