doc:sec-112-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "112(2) Statement of regulatory policy" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) The Parliament intends that the ACMA, in exercising its powers under sections 117, 118, 119, 123, 124, 125, 125AA, 125A and 125B, will act in a manner that, in the opinion of the ACMA, enables public interest considerations to be addressed in a way that does not impose undue financial and administrative burdens on participants in sections of the telecommunications industry, the telemarketing industry or the fax marketing industry." ;
    cof:pageNumber "151"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-112-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "112(3) Statement of regulatory policy"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-112-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) In determining whether public interest considerations are being addressed in a way that does not impose undue financial and administrative burdens on participants in sections of the telecommunications industry (other than electronic messaging service providers), the ACMA must have regard to:  (a) the number of customers who would be likely to benefit from the code or standard concerned; and" ;
    skos:definition "(3) In determining whether public interest considerations are being addressed in a way that does not impose undue financial and administrative burdens on participants in sections of the telecommunications industry (other than electronic messaging service providers), the ACMA must have regard to:  (a) the number of customers who would be likely to benefit from the code or standard concerned; and"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "0013ee57c1f4b1720f1613816351cea454b9aadfd35b7a113ddd050220e2cab1" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-112 ;
    cof:pageNumber "151"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "ACMA must consider public interest when determining burdens on telecommunications industry participants." ;
