concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-122a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "122A De-registering industry codes and provisions of industry codes"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-122a ;
    values:originalText "(1) The ACMA may remove from the Register of industry codes kept under section 136:  (a) an industry code; or  (b) a provision of an industry code.  (2) An industry code ceases to be registered when it is removed from the Register.  (3) If the ACMA removes a provision of an industry code from the Register, this Part has effect in relation to things occurring after the removal of the provision as if the code registered under this Part did not include the provision removed.   Industry codes and industry standards  Part 6 Industry standards  Division 5  Section 123  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The ACMA may remove from the Register of industry codes kept under section 136:  (a) an industry code; or  (b) a provision of an industry code.  (2) An industry code ceases to be registered when it is removed from the Register.  (3) If the ACMA removes a provision of an industry code from the Register, this Part has effect in relation to things occurring after the removal of the provision as if the code registered under this Part did not include the provision removed.   Industry codes and industry standards  Part 6 Industry standards  Division 5  Section 123  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "2744f46937ca2165da0fbf3122a740e1fa6b130b1422ca552313ae0886a7449d" ;
    cof:pageNumber "172"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-122a-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-122a-ss-2 ;
