concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-124 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "124 ACMA may determine industry standard where no industry"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-124 ;
    values:originalText "body or association formed  (1) This section applies if:  (a) the ACMA is satisfied that a particular section of the telecommunications industry, the telemarketing industry or the fax marketing industry is not represented by a body or association; and  (b) the ACMA has published a notice under subsection 119(1) relating to that section of the industry; and  (c) that notice:  (i) states that, if such a body or association were to come into existence within a particular period, the ACMA would be likely to give a notice to that body or association under subsection 118(1); and  (ii) sets out one or more matters relating to the telecommunications activities, telemarketing activities or fax marketing activities, as the case may be, of the participants in that section of the industry; and  (d) no such body or association comes into existence within that period; and  (e) the ACMA is satisfied that it is necessary or convenient for the ACMA to determine a standard in order to:  (i) provide appropriate community safeguards in relation to that matter or those matters; or  (ii) otherwise regulate adequately participants in that section of the industry in relation to that matter or those matters.  (2) The ACMA may, by legislative instrument, determine a standard that applies to participants in that section of the industry and deals with that matter or those matters. A standard under this subsection is to be known as an industry standard.   Industry codes and industry standards  Part 6 Industry standards  Division 5  Section 125  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026" ;
    skos:definition "body or association formed  (1) This section applies if:  (a) the ACMA is satisfied that a particular section of the telecommunications industry, the telemarketing industry or the fax marketing industry is not represented by a body or association; and  (b) the ACMA has published a notice under subsection 119(1) relating to that section of the industry; and  (c) that notice:  (i) states that, if such a body or association were to come into existence within a particular period, the ACMA would be likely to give a notice to that body or association under subsection 118(1); and  (ii) sets out one or more matters relating to the telecommunications activities, telemarketing activities or fax marketing activities, as the case may be, of the participants in that section of the industry; and  (d) no such body or association comes into existence within that period; and  (e) the ACMA is satisfied that it is necessary or convenient for the ACMA to determine a standard in order to:  (i) provide appropriate community safeguards in relation to that matter or those matters; or  (ii) otherwise regulate adequately participants in that section of the industry in relation to that matter or those matters.  (2) The ACMA may, by legislative instrument, determine a standard that applies to participants in that section of the industry and deals with that matter or those matters. A standard under this subsection is to be known as an industry standard.   Industry codes and industry standards  Part 6 Industry standards  Division 5  Section 125  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "314ad295b7998369a92225dd463d335b19881ef926a0ded6213a758c1c4d08f6" ;
    cof:pageNumber "174"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-124-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-124-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
