concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-125aa a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "125AA ACMA must determine an industry standard if directed by"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-125aa ;
    values:originalText "the Minister  (1) The ACMA may, by legislative instrument, determine a standard that:  (a) applies to participants in a particular section of the telecommunications industry; and  (b) deals with one or more matters relating to the telecommunications activities of those participants. Note 1: For examples of matters that may be dealt with by industry standards, see section 113. Note 2: For variation and revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.  (2) A standard under subsection (1) is to be known as an industry standard.  (3) If the ACMA is satisfied that a body or association represents that section of the telecommunications industry, the ACMA must consult the body or association before determining a standard under subsection (1).  (4) The Minister may, in writing, direct the ACMA to:  (a) determine a standard under subsection (1) that:   Industry codes and industry standards  Part 6 Industry standards  Division 5  Section 125A  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (i) applies to participants in a specified section of the telecommunications industry; and  (ii) deals with one or more specified matters relating to the telecommunications activities of those participants; and  (b) do so within a specified period.  (5) The ACMA must not determine a standard under subsection (1) unless it does so in accordance with a direction under subsection (4)." ;
    skos:definition "the Minister  (1) The ACMA may, by legislative instrument, determine a standard that:  (a) applies to participants in a particular section of the telecommunications industry; and  (b) deals with one or more matters relating to the telecommunications activities of those participants. Note 1: For examples of matters that may be dealt with by industry standards, see section 113. Note 2: For variation and revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.  (2) A standard under subsection (1) is to be known as an industry standard.  (3) If the ACMA is satisfied that a body or association represents that section of the telecommunications industry, the ACMA must consult the body or association before determining a standard under subsection (1).  (4) The Minister may, in writing, direct the ACMA to:  (a) determine a standard under subsection (1) that:   Industry codes and industry standards  Part 6 Industry standards  Division 5  Section 125A  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (i) applies to participants in a specified section of the telecommunications industry; and  (ii) deals with one or more specified matters relating to the telecommunications activities of those participants; and  (b) do so within a specified period.  (5) The ACMA must not determine a standard under subsection (1) unless it does so in accordance with a direction under subsection (4)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "e115b5c94ba427ff5d8c6333a58aad5e160e1c74042b853cbb605fae46e27b37" ;
    cof:pageNumber "176"^^xsd:integer ;
