concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-136a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "136A Application for eligibility for reimbursement of costs of"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-136a ;
    values:originalText "development or variation of consumer-related industry code  (1) If a body or association proposes to develop or vary an industry code that:  (a) applies to participants in a particular section of the telecommunications industry; and  (b) deals with one or more matters relating to the telecommunications activities of those participants; and  (c) deals wholly or mainly with one or more matters relating to the relationship between carriage service providers and their retail customers; the body or association may apply to the ACMA for a declaration that the body or association is eligible for reimbursement of refundable costs incurred by it in developing the code or varying the code, as the case may be. Note: For refundable cost, see section 136E. Form of application etc.  (2) An application must be:  (a) in writing; and  (b) in accordance with the form approved in writing by the ACMA; and  (c) accompanied by:  (i) an estimate of the total of the refundable costs likely to be incurred by the body or association in developing the code or varying the code, as the case may be; and  (ii) a statement breaking down that estimate into categories of refundable costs." ;
    skos:definition "development or variation of consumer-related industry code  (1) If a body or association proposes to develop or vary an industry code that:  (a) applies to participants in a particular section of the telecommunications industry; and  (b) deals with one or more matters relating to the telecommunications activities of those participants; and  (c) deals wholly or mainly with one or more matters relating to the relationship between carriage service providers and their retail customers; the body or association may apply to the ACMA for a declaration that the body or association is eligible for reimbursement of refundable costs incurred by it in developing the code or varying the code, as the case may be. Note: For refundable cost, see section 136E. Form of application etc.  (2) An application must be:  (a) in writing; and  (b) in accordance with the form approved in writing by the ACMA; and  (c) accompanied by:  (i) an estimate of the total of the refundable costs likely to be incurred by the body or association in developing the code or varying the code, as the case may be; and  (ii) a statement breaking down that estimate into categories of refundable costs."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "3da613e0846196cfd2e167f92ad163af49afee14ce1253d0c811a5dc679e120f" ;
    cof:pageNumber "185"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-136a-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-136a-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-act-1997.pdf> ;
    dc:source "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.185" .
doc:sec-136a a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "136A Application for eligibility for reimbursement of costs of" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "development or variation of consumer-related industry code  (1) If a body or association proposes to develop or vary an industry code that:  (a) applies to participants in a particular section of the telecommunications industry; and  (b) deals with one or more matters relating to the telecommunications activities of those participants; and  (c) deals wholly or mainly with one or more matters relating to the relationship between carriage service providers and their retail customers; the body or association may apply to the ACMA for a declaration that the body or association is eligible for reimbursement of refundable costs incurred by it in developing the code or varying the code, as the case may be. Note: For refundable cost, see section 136E. Form of application etc.  (2) An application must be:  (a) in writing; and  (b) in accordance with the form approved in writing by the ACMA; and  (c) accompanied by:  (i) an estimate of the total of the refundable costs likely to be incurred by the body or association in developing the code or varying the code, as the case may be; and  (ii) a statement breaking down that estimate into categories of refundable costs." ;
    cof:pageNumber "185"^^xsd:integer .

