concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-142bd a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "142BD Designated carriage service"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-142bd ;
    values:originalText "(1) For the purposes of this Part, designated carriage service means:  (a) if a carriage service is specified in an instrument under subsection (2)—that carriage service; or  (b) otherwise—a Layer 2 bitstream service.  (2) The ACCC may, by legislative instrument, specify a carriage service for the purposes of paragraph (1)(a).  (3) The ACCC must not specify a carriage service under subsection (2) unless:  (a) the carriage service enables end-users to download communications; and  (b) the download transmission speed of the carriage service is normally 25 megabits per second or more; and" ;
    skos:definition "(1) For the purposes of this Part, designated carriage service means:  (a) if a carriage service is specified in an instrument under subsection (2)—that carriage service; or  (b) otherwise—a Layer 2 bitstream service.  (2) The ACCC may, by legislative instrument, specify a carriage service for the purposes of paragraph (1)(a).  (3) The ACCC must not specify a carriage service under subsection (2) unless:  (a) the carriage service enables end-users to download communications; and  (b) the download transmission speed of the carriage service is normally 25 megabits per second or more; and"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "889b175a05d109793072d52d7285f6a3a17235e633455dae77c2984cfd84c3d8" ;
    cof:pageNumber "199"^^xsd:integer ;
