concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-147 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "147 Exemption—gas supply bodies"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-147 ;
    values:originalText "(1) Subsections 142C(2) and 143(2) do not apply if:  (a) the eligible service is a carriage service, and the sole use of the carriage service is use by a gas supply body to carry communications necessary or desirable for:  (i) managing the transmission or distribution of natural gas in a pipeline; or  (ii) charging for the supply of natural gas transmitted or distributed in a pipeline; or  (b) the eligible service is a service that facilitates the supply of a carriage service covered by paragraph (a) of this section.  (2) Paragraph (1)(a) does not apply to a carriage service supplied to a gas supply body unless the carriage service is supplied on the basis that the gas supply body must not re-supply the carriage service." ;
    skos:definition "(1) Subsections 142C(2) and 143(2) do not apply if:  (a) the eligible service is a carriage service, and the sole use of the carriage service is use by a gas supply body to carry communications necessary or desirable for:  (i) managing the transmission or distribution of natural gas in a pipeline; or  (ii) charging for the supply of natural gas transmitted or distributed in a pipeline; or  (b) the eligible service is a service that facilitates the supply of a carriage service covered by paragraph (a) of this section.  (2) Paragraph (1)(a) does not apply to a carriage service supplied to a gas supply body unless the carriage service is supplied on the basis that the gas supply body must not re-supply the carriage service."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "238d251f2a553fbf283008d2101dc1d5bbb5ad3b250dbb10efa5069b622b54a8" ;
    cof:pageNumber "221"^^xsd:integer ;
