    cof:title "151 Exemption—State or Territory road authorities" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) Subsections 142C(2) and 143(2) do not apply if:   Local access lines  Part 8 Exemptions  Division 2A  Section 151  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (a) the eligible service is a carriage service, and the sole use of the carriage service is use by a State or Territory road authority to carry communications necessary or desirable for the management or control of road traffic; or  (b) the eligible service is a service that facilitates the supply of a carriage service covered by paragraph (a) of this section.  (2) Paragraph (1)(a) does not apply to a carriage service supplied to a State or Territory road authority unless the carriage service is supplied on the basis that the State or Territory road authority must not re-supply the carriage service." ;
    cof:pageNumber "222"^^xsd:integer .

