    skos:definition "(2) If:  (a) the ACCC has given a notice under section 151W revoking a joint functional separation undertaking; and  (b) the revocation has not taken effect; the ACCC may, by written notice given to a person who gave the undertaking jointly with one or more other persons, direct the person:  (c) to give the ACCC:  (i) a report about the person’s compliance with the undertaking; or  (ii) information about the person’s compliance with the undertaking; or  (iii) a report about action that the person has taken, is taking, or proposes to take for the purpose of ensuring that the person complies with sections 142C and 143 after the revocation takes effect; or  (iv) information about action that the person has taken, is taking, or proposes to take for the purpose of ensuring that the person complies with sections 142C and 143 after the revocation takes effect; and  (d) to do so within the period specified in the direction. Note: See section 151ZJ (self-incrimination)."@en ;
