    values:originalText "(1) If a functional separation undertaking given by a person is in force, the person must comply with the undertaking. Note: See also section 142B. Ancillary contraventions  (2) A person must not:  (a) aid, abet, counsel or procure a contravention of subsection (1); or  (b) induce, whether by threats or promises or otherwise, a contravention of subsection (1); or  (c) be in any way, directly or indirectly, knowingly concerned in, or party to, a contravention of subsection (1); or   Local access lines  Part 8 Functional separation undertakings  Division 2B  Section 151ZE  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (d) conspire with others to effect a contravention of subsection (1). Civil penalty provisions  (3) Subsections (1) and (2) are civil penalty provisions. Note: Part 31 provides for pecuniary penalties for breaches of civil penalty provisions." ;
