doc:sec-151zm-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "151ZM(3) Functions and powers of the Australian Competition" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) If the Australian Competition Tribunal sets aside a decision of the ACCC under section 151F to reject a functional separation undertaking, subsection 151F(5) has effect as if the undertaking had been received by the ACCC immediately after the decision was set aside. Note: This subsection resets the start of the 3-month decision-making period set out in subsection 151F(5)." ;
    cof:pageNumber "276"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-151zm-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "151ZM(4) Functions and powers of the Australian Competition"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-151zm-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) If the Australian Competition Tribunal sets aside a decision of the ACCC under section 151T to reject a variation, subsection 151T(5) has effect as if the variation had been received by the ACCC immediately after the decision was set aside. Note: This subsection resets the start of the 3-month decision-making period set out in subsection 151T(5).   Local access lines  Part 8 Other provisions  Division 3  Section 151ZN  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  Conduct of review" ;
