    values:originalText "(2) A person who has been an eligible person must not disclose or use any information or document that:  (a) relates to a matter mentioned in paragraph (1)(a); and  (b) came to the person’s knowledge, or into the person’s possession:  (i) if the person was a carrier or carriage service provider— in connection with the person’s business as such a carrier or provider; or  (ii) if the person was an employee of a carrier or carriage service provider—because the person was employed by the carrier or provider in connection with its business as such a carrier or provider; or  (iii) if the person was a telecommunications contractor—in connection with the person’s business as such a contractor; or  (iv) if the person was an employee of a telecommunications contractor—because the person was employed by the contractor in connection with its business as such a contractor. Offence" ;
    cof:pageNumber "296"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-276-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "276(3) Primary disclosure/use offence—eligible persons"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-276-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) A person who contravenes this section commits an offence punishable on conviction by imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years. Note 1: This section is subject to the exceptions in Division 3 of this Part and in Chapter 4 of the Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979. Note 2: See also sections 4AA and 4B of the Crimes Act 1914." ;
