    cof:title "286 Calls to emergency service number" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Division 2 does not prohibit a disclosure by a person of information or a document if:  (a) the information or document came to the person’s knowledge, or into the person’s possession, because of a call to an emergency service number; and  (b) the information, or the contents of the document, consists of any or all of the following:  (i) a name;  (ii) a telephone number;  (iii) an address;  (iv) a location;  (v) the matter or matters raised by the call; and  (c) the disclosure is made to:  (i) an emergency service; or  (ii) a service for despatching an emergency service; or   Protection of communications  Part 13 Exceptions to primary disclosure/use offences  Division 3  Section 287  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (iv) an emergency call person; or  for purposes connected with dealing with the matter or matters raised by the call." ;
    cof:pageNumber "312"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-287 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "287 Threat to person’s life or health"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-287 ;
    values:originalText "Division 2 does not prohibit a disclosure or use by a person (the first person) of information or a document if:  (a) the information or document relates to the affairs or personal particulars (including any unlisted telephone number or any address) of another person; and  (ab) it is unreasonable or impracticable to obtain the other person’s consent to the disclosure or use; and  (b) the first person believes on reasonable grounds that the disclosure or use is reasonably necessary to prevent or lessen a serious threat to the life or health of a person." ;
    skos:definition "Division 2 does not prohibit a disclosure or use by a person (the first person) of information or a document if:  (a) the information or document relates to the affairs or personal particulars (including any unlisted telephone number or any address) of another person; and  (ab) it is unreasonable or impracticable to obtain the other person’s consent to the disclosure or use; and  (b) the first person believes on reasonable grounds that the disclosure or use is reasonably necessary to prevent or lessen a serious threat to the life or health of a person."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "fde2c47afd2ea6412847423b7ebec987135757fa7b9dc778d9f7a3b8485bec96" ;
    cof:pageNumber "313"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Disclosure or use of information is allowed under certain conditions to prevent a serious threat to life or health." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
