concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-295a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "295A ACMA to make integrated public number database scheme"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-295a ;
    values:originalText "The ACMA must, by legislative instrument, make a scheme (the integrated public number database scheme) for the granting of authorisations for the purposes of paragraph 285(1A)(d). Note 1: The ACMA may make determinations fixing charges for any matter in relation to which expenses are incurred by the ACMA under the scheme: see section 60 of the Australian Communications and Media Authority Act 2005. Note 2: Various decisions under the scheme are reviewable: see section 555 and paragraphs 1(ma) to (md) of Schedule 4." ;
    skos:definition "The ACMA must, by legislative instrument, make a scheme (the integrated public number database scheme) for the granting of authorisations for the purposes of paragraph 285(1A)(d). Note 1: The ACMA may make determinations fixing charges for any matter in relation to which expenses are incurred by the ACMA under the scheme: see section 60 of the Australian Communications and Media Authority Act 2005. Note 2: Various decisions under the scheme are reviewable: see section 555 and paragraphs 1(ma) to (md) of Schedule 4."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "0fa3859277ffc78f226da000e1ed992ac4f4a1bf8e1dd21ff91c8af52ebfda3b" ;
    cof:pageNumber "320"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "ACMA must make integrated public number database scheme" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-act-1997.pdf> ;
    dc:source "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.320" ;
    cml:asserts concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-295a-norm .
concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-295a-norm a values:Undertaking ;
    cml:modality cml:Deontic ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-295a ;
    values:deonticStatus values:HeuristicDerived ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .
doc:sec-295a a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "295A ACMA to make integrated public number database scheme" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "The ACMA must, by legislative instrument, make a scheme (the integrated public number database scheme) for the granting of authorisations for the purposes of paragraph 285(1A)(d). Note 1: The ACMA may make determinations fixing charges for any matter in relation to which expenses are incurred by the ACMA under the scheme: see section 60 of the Australian Communications and Media Authority Act 2005. Note 2: Various decisions under the scheme are reviewable: see section 555 and paragraphs 1(ma) to (md) of Schedule 4." ;
    cof:pageNumber "320"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-295b a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "295B Scheme must deal with certain matters"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-295b ;
    values:originalText "(1) The scheme must make provision for and in relation to the following matters:  (a) the making of applications for authorisations;  (b) the assessment of applications;  (c) the period for which authorisations are to be in force;  (d) the notification of decisions under the scheme (including to the person who maintains the integrated public number database referred to in paragraph 285(1A)(a)).  (2) The scheme must require an applicant for an authorisation to specify the purpose for which the authorisation is sought. Note: The relevant purposes are purposes connected with the publication and maintenance of a public number directory or with the conduct of particular research.   Protection of communications  Part 13 Integrated public number database authorisations  Division 3A  Section 295C  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The scheme must make provision for and in relation to the following matters:  (a) the making of applications for authorisations;  (b) the assessment of applications;  (c) the period for which authorisations are to be in force;  (d) the notification of decisions under the scheme (including to the person who maintains the integrated public number database referred to in paragraph 285(1A)(a)).  (2) The scheme must require an applicant for an authorisation to specify the purpose for which the authorisation is sought. Note: The relevant purposes are purposes connected with the publication and maintenance of a public number directory or with the conduct of particular research.   Protection of communications  Part 13 Integrated public number database authorisations  Division 3A  Section 295C  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "e700af05f80ad2ffcc1ae36d9383afed06048f2c9478d20cec97a1c931004f46" ;
    cof:pageNumber "320"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-295b-ss-1 ;
