    values:originalText "management persons  An emergency management person commits an offence if:  (a) the person uses or discloses relevant information; and  (b) the use or disclosure is not permitted under section 295V. Penalty: Imprisonment for 2 years." ;
    cof:pageNumber "328"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-295za a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "295ZA Offence—use or disclosure of information by other persons"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-295za ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) information is disclosed to the person as permitted by subsection 295V(1) or (2) or 295W(1); and  (b) the person uses or discloses the information; and  (c) the use or disclosure referred to in paragraph (b) of this subsection is not for a purpose connected with persons being alerted to the emergency or likely emergency concerned. Penalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.  (2) A person commits an offence if:  (a) information is disclosed to the person as permitted by subsection 295V(3) or 295W(2); and  (b) the person uses or discloses the information; and  (c) the use or disclosure referred to in paragraph (b) of this subsection is not for the purpose of reasonable testing of whether, in the event of an emergency occurring, persons would be able to be alerted to that emergency. Penalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.  (3) A person commits an offence if:  (a) information is disclosed to the person as permitted by subsection 295V(4) or 295W(3); and   Protection of communications  Part 13 Emergency warnings  Division 3B  Section 295ZB  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (b) the person uses or discloses the information; and  (c) the use or disclosure referred to in paragraph (b) of this subsection is not for a purpose connected with persons being alerted to an emergency or a likely emergency. Penalty: Imprisonment for 2 years." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) information is disclosed to the person as permitted by subsection 295V(1) or (2) or 295W(1); and  (b) the person uses or discloses the information; and  (c) the use or disclosure referred to in paragraph (b) of this subsection is not for a purpose connected with persons being alerted to the emergency or likely emergency concerned. Penalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.  (2) A person commits an offence if:  (a) information is disclosed to the person as permitted by subsection 295V(3) or 295W(2); and  (b) the person uses or discloses the information; and  (c) the use or disclosure referred to in paragraph (b) of this subsection is not for the purpose of reasonable testing of whether, in the event of an emergency occurring, persons would be able to be alerted to that emergency. Penalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.  (3) A person commits an offence if:  (a) information is disclosed to the person as permitted by subsection 295V(4) or 295W(3); and   Protection of communications  Part 13 Emergency warnings  Division 3B  Section 295ZB  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (b) the person uses or discloses the information; and  (c) the use or disclosure referred to in paragraph (b) of this subsection is not for a purpose connected with persons being alerted to an emergency or a likely emergency. Penalty: Imprisonment for 2 years."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "03344987ce14beae64af470c87ecd84a28b5584095c56cedba074163b8c5fc04" ;
    cof:pageNumber "328"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-295za-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-295za-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-295za-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
