    values:originalText "(1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) information is disclosed to the person as permitted by subsection 295V(1) or (2) or 295W(1); and  (b) the person uses or discloses the information; and  (c) the use or disclosure referred to in paragraph (b) of this subsection is not for a purpose connected with persons being alerted to the emergency or likely emergency concerned. Penalty: Imprisonment for 2 years." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) information is disclosed to the person as permitted by subsection 295V(1) or (2) or 295W(1); and  (b) the person uses or discloses the information; and  (c) the use or disclosure referred to in paragraph (b) of this subsection is not for a purpose connected with persons being alerted to the emergency or likely emergency concerned. Penalty: Imprisonment for 2 years."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "568a1e052d84544d915b427c28d8f08c8848d862427360380047d12d6b3a805a" ;
