concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-295za-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "295ZA(2) Offence—use or disclosure of information by other persons"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-295za-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) A person commits an offence if:  (a) information is disclosed to the person as permitted by subsection 295V(3) or 295W(2); and  (b) the person uses or discloses the information; and  (c) the use or disclosure referred to in paragraph (b) of this subsection is not for the purpose of reasonable testing of whether, in the event of an emergency occurring, persons would be able to be alerted to that emergency. Penalty: Imprisonment for 2 years." ;
    skos:definition "(2) A person commits an offence if:  (a) information is disclosed to the person as permitted by subsection 295V(3) or 295W(2); and  (b) the person uses or discloses the information; and  (c) the use or disclosure referred to in paragraph (b) of this subsection is not for the purpose of reasonable testing of whether, in the event of an emergency occurring, persons would be able to be alerted to that emergency. Penalty: Imprisonment for 2 years."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "003197d2e74a2f897d1e267477c7a9d91ca09389dfa63fcc391fc4b954f95890" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-295za ;
    cof:pageNumber "328"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Disclosing or using information without permission is an offence." ;
