concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-299 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "299 Assisting the ACMA, the eSafety Commissioner, the ACCC or"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-299 ;
    values:originalText "the Telecommunications Industry Ombudsman  (1) If information or a document is disclosed to a person as permitted by subsection 284(1) or this subsection, the person must not disclose or use the information or document except for the purpose of, or in connection with, the carrying out of the ACMA’s functions and powers.  (1A) If information or a document is disclosed to a person as permitted by subsection 284(1A) or this subsection, the person must not disclose or use the information or document except for the purpose of, or in connection with, the carrying out of the eSafety Commissioner’s functions and powers.  (2) If information or a document is disclosed to a person as permitted by subsection 284(2) or this subsection, the person must not" ;
    skos:definition "the Telecommunications Industry Ombudsman  (1) If information or a document is disclosed to a person as permitted by subsection 284(1) or this subsection, the person must not disclose or use the information or document except for the purpose of, or in connection with, the carrying out of the ACMA’s functions and powers.  (1A) If information or a document is disclosed to a person as permitted by subsection 284(1A) or this subsection, the person must not disclose or use the information or document except for the purpose of, or in connection with, the carrying out of the eSafety Commissioner’s functions and powers.  (2) If information or a document is disclosed to a person as permitted by subsection 284(2) or this subsection, the person must not"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "205f9ce45bbf457d0936d9c0aefc2bada3efaaae8da393227551b1f724e3855b" ;
    cof:pageNumber "331"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-299-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-299-ss-1a ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-299-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-act-1997.pdf> ;
    dc:source "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.331" .
doc:sec-299 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "299 Assisting the ACMA, the eSafety Commissioner, the ACCC or" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "the Telecommunications Industry Ombudsman  (1) If information or a document is disclosed to a person as permitted by subsection 284(1) or this subsection, the person must not disclose or use the information or document except for the purpose of, or in connection with, the carrying out of the ACMA’s functions and powers.  (1A) If information or a document is disclosed to a person as permitted by subsection 284(1A) or this subsection, the person must not disclose or use the information or document except for the purpose of, or in connection with, the carrying out of the eSafety Commissioner’s functions and powers.  (2) If information or a document is disclosed to a person as permitted by subsection 284(2) or this subsection, the person must not" ;
    cof:pageNumber "331"^^xsd:integer .

