doc:sec-309-ss-1a a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "309(1A) Monitoring by the Information Commissioner" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1A) The function conferred on the Information Commissioner by subsection (1) is a privacy function for the purposes of the Australian Information Commissioner Act 2010." ;
    cof:pageNumber "342"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-309-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "309(2) Monitoring by the Information Commissioner"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-309-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) In particular, the function conferred on the Information Commissioner by subsection (1) includes monitoring:  (a) whether a record made under section 306 or 306A sets out a statement of the grounds for a disclosure; and  (b) whether that statement is covered by Division 3 of this Part or Chapter 4 of the Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979 (which deal with exceptions)." ;
    skos:definition "(2) In particular, the function conferred on the Information Commissioner by subsection (1) includes monitoring:  (a) whether a record made under section 306 or 306A sets out a statement of the grounds for a disclosure; and  (b) whether that statement is covered by Division 3 of this Part or Chapter 4 of the Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979 (which deal with exceptions)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "336b9db6ad88dbf3dc71bc4866393e15263404c31ed7fe19b63bb2fa432d6b0d" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-309 ;
    cof:pageNumber "342"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "The Information Commissioner must monitor certain records." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
